pysisyphus 1.0.0: 0003-gs-bracketed-lambda

What: Gonzalez–Schlegel finds λ by a bracketed search (scipy brentq) below the lowest eigenvalue, where the constraint function rises monotonically from −r² to +∞ so the root is unique, instead of Newton's method from a guess; no root raises IRCIntegratorFailure.
Test: Same replay: Newton's search fails on the BFGS Hessian (pysisyphus 1.0.0 then calls the IRC converged); the bracketed search returns a point on the hypersphere (radius error 3e-16); the SN2 validation path (939 gradients) had no failed search.

